  "reasoning_content": "We need answer user: \"Write a detailed tutorial on implementing a bounded LRU cache in Python using collections.OrderedDict. Include a complete class, explain get and put behavior, discuss edge cases, and include tests. Continue with a worked example and complexity analysis. Be precise and use meaningful prose and code.\"\n\nNeed produce final answer detailed tutorial. Need include complete class, get/put behavior, edge cases, tests, worked example, complexity. Use Python code. Need be precise.\n\nLet's plan.\n\nTopic: bounded LRU cache using collections.OrderedDict.\n\nWe can implement class LRUCache:\n- __init__(self, capacity: int): if capacity <=0? Edge case. Could raise ValueError or handle no storage. Need discuss. For bounded LRU, capacity positive. If capacity 0, no items can be stored; get returns None, put discards. We can choose to raise ValueError for capacity < 0 and allow 0? Better precise: if capacity < 0 raise ValueError; if capacity == 0, cache stores nothing. Or require positive. Let's implement robust: if capacity < 0: raise ValueError; if capacity == 0: self._capacity=0; self._cache=OrderedDict(); return. But put with capacity 0 should not store. get returns None.\n\n- get(key, default=None): if key in cache: move_to_end(key); return cache[key]; else return default. Need note default can be None or sentinel. If cached value is None, get returns None; to distinguish miss use sentinel or contains. We can include sentinel.\n\n- put(key, value): if key in cache: update value and move_to_end(key) (most recently used). Else: if len(cache) >= capacity: if capacity == 0: return; popitem(last=False) evict least recently used (first item). Then cache[key]=value. If capacity positive.\n\nOrderedDict maintains insertion order; move_to_end(key, last=True) moves to end. popitem(last=False) removes first (LRU). For MRU? We can mention.\n\nNeed include tests. Use unittest or pytest. Could include both? Use unittest for standard library. Tests:\n- test_get_missing_returns_default\n- test_put_and_get\n- test_update_existing_key_moves_to_recent\n- test_evicts_least_recently_used_when_full\n- test_get_updates_recency\n- test_capacity_zero\n- test_negative_capacity_raises\n- test_default_value",
